# WHAT ENTERS (committed to `src/` on fix/retirement in this same change):
#   - parser (`macro_expand.tks`): a pattern-position `@Type()` that expands to a union WHOSE OWN MEMBER
#     is itself a union — the shape §9.D leaves nested when a union-of-unions is inlined (e.g.
#     `@TStatement()` sitting inside `@TItem()`'s lowering body) — now contributes, for that nested
#     member, a bindingless `GroupBindPattern` OPTION rather than flattening the member's cases into the
#     parent option list (`union_member_option`). The candidate the checker then builds keeps the member
#     nested, exactly as the TYPE side keeps it nested (`resolve_type`'s `UnionType` arm does not flatten).
#   - checker (`match.tks`): `group_option_type` resolves such a nested `GroupBindPattern` option to its
#     own anonymous sub-union (`group_candidate`), so `group_bind_subunion` matches the subject's boxed
#     nested `Variant` member by `type_eq` — no re-tag, no re-box (§9.D nested-group byte-identity).
#   Carried forward from the prior reseeds: §9.D CR1 (box recursive members of a bare inline union),
#   CR2 (structure-encode the inline-union generic-instance mangle in checker + codegen), CR3 (`@Type()`
#   in a group-bind pattern position via `MacroPattern`), §14 A0-A4 / B1-B5, §14 Form 2 parametric
#   type-macros, §9.D capabilities (a)/(b)/(c), the checker self-qualification fix, and the §9.D sweep so
#   far (30 unions retired before this reseed).
